resizeLightT -- forms step 6, stroke 4's last piece (Tony, 2026-11-12): Layout writes layoutFrame as ONE WHOLE WRITE, on
firstLight, with a mock resize: PDF before, resize, PDF after. Rows in genLadder/formsPop.sh.

layoutFrame is utilities' field. The form's request names it as frame:=, and onResize listens to it and calls redrawForm.
The mock resize is the one statement Layout's write amounts to: layoutFrame = rgBig, a field holding x y width height.
That one write carries all four values and fires onResize once.

RG-1  before: firstLight as declared, 400x200, by a plain call. Four points, firstPdfT's PD-1.
RG-2  the resize to 600x300: one run of the listener; the page is 600x300; words re-flows from 4 lines to 3; heading, words, space and ok are at their new
      places, and where ok was at 400x200, (390,190), is now words' white.
RG-3  A RESIZE READS LIKE A FRESH RUN: the same form laid out at 600x300 by a plain call with the frame in the request,
      no listening. The page and the five points are RG-2's exactly, and the text drawn is the same count.
RG-4  resized back to 400x200 by the same road: a second run, and the page and points are RG-1's exactly.
RG-5  the definition still declares 400x200.

WHAT THE LISTENING WORK NEEDED TO PASS (found here, cured in GroupItem.setContent): a whole-field assignment into a
listened-to field copied the list over the field's listener list -- so the listener was gone after one write -- and told
nobody, because only a value write notified. setContent now keeps the listener list across the list copy and tells the
listeners once, after all four values have arrived. Before the cure RG-2 read runs 0.

RE-PINNED 2026-11-13 (G2 stroke 1b): firstLight holds the descriptions form in its lower half (inside, height=50%) and is declared
400x400, so the two frames are 400x400 and 600x600 (they were 400x200 and 600x300). heading, words, bar and ok keep the frames
they had at both sizes, so every point and line count above reads as it did; only the page sizes in the rows changed.
